From: DEEPX Performance Guide
Subject: [dx_app] Decouple live display from capture/inference submission (AsyncDetectionRunner)

Problem
-------
With a live preview window enabled, cv::imshow()/cv::waitKey() were polled
on the SAME thread that reads video frames and submits them for async NPU
inference. Because cv::waitKey() always fully services the GUI event queue
(regardless of the ms argument passed to it), every GUI poll injected extra
delay directly into the frame-read-and-submit loop, starving the NPU of new
work. Measured effect: Overall FPS dropped from ~310 (--no-display) to
~119 with the preview window on, and "Infer Inflight Avg" collapsed from
6.0 to 1.6.

Fix
---
1. Move frame read + preprocess + RunAsync submission onto its own thread
   (captureThr), throttled only by the existing back-pressure mechanism
   (metrics_.waitForSlot()) -- exactly like the --no-display path already
   was. The main thread becomes a dedicated display pump, decoupled from
   capture speed.
2. Make the rendered-frame hand-off to the main-thread display a small,
   drop-oldest queue (2 slots) instead of a 100-slot blocking queue, so a
   slow/backed-up preview can never gate capture or inference -- it just
   skips stale frames (mirrors AsyncPoseRunner's existing pattern).
3. Pass pump_events=false to showOutput() from pollDisplay(), since
   pollDisplay() already pumps GUI events itself right after -- avoiding a
   double pump per frame (common_util.hpp's own showOutput() doc comment
   already calls this out; AsyncDetectionRunner just wasn't doing it).

Measured result (yolo26-n_640x640.dxnn, snowboard.mp4, live preview on):
  Overall FPS         : 119.3  ->  215.2   (~1.8x)
  Infer Inflight Avg  :   1.6  ->    4.5
  Inference throughput: 121.4  ->  222.1 FPS
--no-display path is unaffected (measured ~298-311 FPS before and after).

Apply from the extracted package root, e.g.:
  cd yolo26-standalone/cpp/object_detection/yolo26n
  patch -p1 < 0001-decouple-display-from-capture-submit.patch
  # or: git apply 0001-decouple-display-from-capture-submit.patch
  cd build && make -j$(nproc)

